lively_bends:
Lively Bends

 Lively Bends is a Fabric mod that makes player movement in Minecraft feel more lively, smooth, and expressive while preserving the game's recognizable visual style.

The project is inspired by the legendary Mo' Bends , which transformed Minecraft animations with bending limbs and more natural full-body movement. Unfortunately, the original mod has not supported modern versions of the game for a long time.

That's why Lively Bends was created.

 What does Lively Bends change?

The mod reworks the player's core animations, including:

- walking;
- sprinting;
- sneaking and crouched movement;
- jumping and airborne movement;
- swimming;
- flying;
- combat and weapon animations.

One of its main features is bending arms and legs . Movement affects not only the limbs, but also the torso and other parts of the player model, making the character feel significantly more alive.

